      scholarships: "• <b>One-year Entrance Scholarship</b> — $3,000 (non-renewable). All applicants are automatically considered, on academic achievement alone; McGill's published estimate for consideration for overseas high schools is a minimum A average (approximately 97% or equivalent) over the last two years of full-time study and/or rank in the top 1% of class (IB: 41 subject points; A-Levels: four subjects at A*A*A*A). Meeting the estimate does not guarantee an offer.<br>• <b>Major Entrance Scholarships</b> — $3,000, $5,000 or $10,000 per year, renewable up to 3–4 years; awarded on academic achievement first, followed by demonstrated leadership. Separate application on the Undergraduate Admissions Applicant Portal (opens October 1; deadline January 21 for applicants from schools outside Canada).<br>• <span style=\"opacity:.55\"><b>Major Entrance Scholarship — $12,000-per-year tier</b> — Canadian citizens and legal permanent residents of Canada only. Not open to Indian nationals (the maximum for international students is $10,000 per year).</span><br>• <b>Entrance Bursary Program</b> — need-based support for newly accepted first-year, first-degree students from low- to modest-income families; average offers for US/International students are about $19,000. Apply through McGill Financial Aid within 30 days of your acceptance date.<br>• <span style=\"opacity:.55\"><b>McCall MacBain Scholarship</b> — funds master's and second-entry professional programmes only. Not open to Indian nationals applying for a first undergraduate degree.</span>",
