          icse: "CISCE is treated together with CBSE at UBC — no separate ISC requirements are published. No India application minimum percentage exists on official sources for either board; expect senior Mathematics, Chemistry and Physics (the published Applied Science prerequisites, applied to international curricula as appropriate). ⚠️ An offer can be re-evaluated if final Standard XII results fall below 85%.",
          ib: "Completed IB Diploma, including at least three Higher Level courses; UBC publishes NO IB total-points cut-off. Required: IB Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches SL or HL, or IB Mathematics: Applications and Interpretations HL; IB Chemistry; IB Physics. ⚠️ Academically strong candidates missing either IB Chemistry or IB Physics may be evaluated on a case-by-case basis. (Specializations such as Mechanical or Electrical are chosen after the common first year.)",
          al: "GCSE/GCE standing in at least six academic subject areas, including English, with at least three academic A Levels or six AS Levels. Degree-specific A-Level subjects are NOT published on a retrievable official page; UBC applies its published programme prerequisites (Mathematics, Chemistry, Physics) to international curricula as appropriate. A final grade of A or B in A-Level First Language English or English Literature also meets the English standard."
