          cbse: "⚠️ Computer Science is NOT a direct-entry degree at UBC — you apply to Science (or Arts) and select the Computer Science specialization after first year. (UBC's separate Bachelor of Computer Science is a second-degree programme for students who already hold a bachelor's degree.) The Science application rules therefore apply: UBC publishes NO India application minimum percentage, considers all academic Grade 11 and 12 courses, and an offer is re-evaluated if final Standard XII results fall below 85%.",
          icse: "⚠️ Computer Science is NOT a direct-entry degree at UBC — apply to Science (or Arts) and choose the specialization after first year. CISCE is treated together with CBSE: no separate ISC requirements and no India application minimum percentage are published; the Science route's rules (including the 85% offer-retention condition) apply.",
          ib: "⚠️ Computer Science has no separate IB list — apply to Science (or Arts) and follow that degree's requirements: completed IB Diploma with at least three Higher Level courses, Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches SL or HL (or Applications and Interpretations HL), and one of IB Biology, Chemistry or Physics. UBC publishes NO IB total-points cut-off.",
          al: "⚠️ Computer Science has no separate A-Level list — apply to Science (or Arts): GCSE/GCE standing in at least six academic subject areas, including English, with at least three academic A Levels or six AS Levels. UBC applies its published Science prerequisites (Mathematics plus a science) to international curricula as appropriate."
